<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.8"/>
    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Thirst, frequent urination day and night, tiredness and about 4 kg weight loss over two months, with a random glucose of 246 mg/dL; told by physicians a year ago that he had diabetes, never confirmed with modern tests or treated except by diet. Diabetes to be confirmed and classified (type 2, type 1 or slowly progressive autoimmune diabetes) with A1c, fasting glucose, GAD antibodies and C-peptide: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Raised blood pressure in clinic (138/86, average of two readings) without a diagnosis of hypertension; home readings to be taken: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Long-standing difficulty falling asleep: by his own account he has never been able to fall asleep on getting into bed and lies awake for two hours or more most nights; worse lately with waking to pass urine; rises before dawn for meditation: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Endocrinology consultation in one week, the same day as fasting blood tests, to confirm and classify diabetes (A1c, fasting glucose, GAD antibodies, C-peptide), and advise on treatment that fits his diet, his religious fasts and his travel. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, diabetes type 2, hypertension, hyperlipidemia, CKD and asthma monographs (2026); 2. Diagnosis and Classification of Diabetes: Standards of Care in Diabetes-2026 (2026); 9. Pharmacologic Approaches to Glycemic Treatment: Standards of Care in Diabetes-2026 (2026) [S]</item><item>Diagnostic tests in one week, fasting: A1c, fasting plasma glucose, GAD65 antibodies, C-peptide, urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio, lipid panel, ALT, TSH and vitamin B12; urine ketones negative today; drink water freely while thirsty and avoid waterless fasts until the results are known; return the same day if vomiting, abdominal pain or drowsiness. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, diabetes type 2, hypertension, hyperlipidemia, CKD and asthma monographs (2026); 2. Diagnosis and Classification of Diabetes: Standards of Care in Diabetes-2026 (2026); 9. Pharmacologic Approaches to Glycemic Treatment: Standards of Care in Diabetes-2026 (2026); 4. Comprehensive Medical Evaluation and Assessment of Comorbidities: Standards of Care in Diabetes-2026 (2026) [S]</item><item>Home blood pressure readings twice daily for a week with a validated upper-arm cuff, because clinic readings are raised. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, diabetes type 2, hypertension, hyperlipidemia, CKD and asthma monographs (2026); 10. Cardiovascular Disease and Risk Management: Standards of Care in Diabetes-2026 (2026) [S]</item><item>Insomnia: sleep diary for two weeks, screening for sleep apnea, and cognitive behavioral therapy for insomnia adapted to his pre-dawn meditation; no sleeping tablets, by his preference; nocturia to be reviewed once glucose is treated. Guideline: Management of Chronic Insomnia Disorder in Adults: A Clinical Practice Guideline From the American College of Physicians (2016); Behavioral and psychological treatments for chronic insomnia disorder in adults: an American Academy of Sleep Medicine clinical practice guideline (2021) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
